{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwcyRwQ2L6SLteg2HJqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check the panels render, and the rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\n**Data:** the logs data view is `kibana_sample_data_logs`, with `timestamp` as its time field. Each document is a web request. The fields I used are the response code (`response` and `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `host`, `machine.os`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-2d8f61df Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-2d8f61df-web-logs-overview-b2dc17321402.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-2d8f61df 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents have a `response.keyword` starting with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes. Its id is `af89b457-1253-4821-9b08-7317f1f5b110`. I didn't add any notification action, so it will only show up as an alert in Kibana.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may not fall in the last 5 minutes, in which case the rule won't fire."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1209,"cache_read_input_tokens":19905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1209},"output_tokens":475,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"f4a7e919-0157-446c-815d-65d2dba632ca","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:19:17.048Z","request_id":"req_011CfwcyRkVtdQo7Ba9DfwUk"}
